<title>TURKEY: Turk Akbank 9-mth profits up 136 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Akbank 9-mth profits up 136 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	1,396.61  vs   1,777.22</p>
<p>    Net profit			25,138.94  vs  10,663.30</p>
<p>    Net interest income	   46,121.00  vs  21,316.91</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense    10,597.36  vs   6,185.70</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans	 193.57  vs	24.33</p>
<p>    Loans			    104,290.47  vs  41,052.88</p>
<p>    Deposits			 263,934.35  vs 125,314.63</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		   2,632.26  vs   1,683.32</p>
<p>    Equity			    39,450.34  vs  18,336.78</p>
<p>    Capital			   18,000.00  vs   6,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Akbank T.A.S., one of Turkey's biggest private banks, is largely owned by Sabanci group, one of Turkey's leading industrial conglomerates.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875 EKS</p>
</text>
